  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $10.7B in federal contract spending in FY2026 to date. NASA executed 6,342 awards with an average award size of $1.7M. Obligations fell 32.3% year over year. Annual comparisons show FY26 obligations at $10.7B versus prior fiscal years of $15B in FY21, $15.2B in FY22, $16.1B in FY23, $15B in FY24, and $15.8B in FY25. Research and development work dominates NASA contracting, with Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) totaling $4.1B in FY2026 to date. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $1.7B. CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY received the largest vendor share at $1.7B, followed by THE BOEING COMPANY at $1B and THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC at $469M. Facilities, engineering services, construction, propulsion manufacturing, and air transportation also appear among the top categories and vendors, reflecting a mix of R&D, manufacturing, and support work in the current fiscal year pipeline.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has National Aeronautics and Space Administration contract spending changed recently?",
        "body": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $10.7B in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 32.3% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior-year totals of $15B in FY21, $15.2B in FY22, $16.1B in FY23, $15B in FY24, and $15.8B in FY25. The FY2026 to date total is lower than each of those prior fiscal-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What contract types and industries receive the most NASA dollars?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) received $4.1B in FY2026 to date. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing received $1.7B, and other top categories include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) at $666M and Engineering Services at $660M. Industrial Building Construction, Facilities Support Services, air transportation, propulsion parts manufacturing, and computer services also appear among the top categories."
      }
